r screenshot), or connects one.
The modes: those three kinds of conversation. The code calls them ConversationMode: Add, Change and Connect. They're what I've been calling the three sessions or conversations.
The tools: the functions the model can call in that chat. There are eight:

printer\_identify and printer\_add, which find a printer and save it;
printer\_manual\_setup, which opens OrcaSlicer's full printer list;
printer\_change, which saves a new nozzle size;
printer\_connection\_status, printer\_connect and printer\_manual\_connection, for connecting;
printer\_setup\_finish, which closes the chat.

check if it's true that we currently have 8 tool calls just for setting up printers.  If so, check it against the tool guide to see if this is justified.

